# Kernel config fragment: Userspace I/O (UIO) for the FPGA miner register block.
#
# Enables non-root + interrupt-driven access to the pipelined miner's Avalon-MM
# window via /dev/uio0, as an alternative to the root-only /dev/mem path
# (docs/uio-miner-io-scope.md WS2). multi_v7_defconfig ships neither symbol.
#
# uio_pdrv_genirq binds the "generic-uio" devicetree node
# (socfpga_cyclone5_qmtech_odo.dts) and delivers the WS1 found-nonce interrupt
# (f2h_irq0 line 3 = GIC SPI 75) to userspace. It only matches that compatible
# when the kernel cmdline carries `uio_pdrv_genirq.of_id=generic-uio` — set in
# the boot.scr bootargs (scripts/build-sdcard.sh). Userspace side:
# hps/miner_io_pipe_uio.c.
CONFIG_UIO=y
CONFIG_UIO_PDRV_GENIRQ=y
